// image.jet — the typed `.Oci` container surface (U14, D-JPK-IMAGE1=A), the
// executable spec for `Image` field-checking and capture on the container tier.
//
// `image.<name>` has two referents (D-JPK-IMAGE1): `from: system.<name>` (the
// `.Iso`/`.Qcow`/`.Raw` disk-image tier, `tests/fixtures/jetpack-typed/system.jet`
// covers that shape) or `from: packages.<name>` (the `.Oci` container tier,
// this file). `kind:` is a leading-dot enum value and optional — it's inferred
// from which `from:` keyword is written, but may be stated explicitly too.
//
// `packages: { server: executable }` in `package.jet` (this repo's own manifest
// pattern, mirrored here inline via the fixture's own declared package) is
// what an `.Oci` image's `from:` cross-checks against (E1267 rejects a
// `library`-kind or undeclared package).
//
// `expose`/`env_vars`/`files` are `.Oci`-only fields: exposed TCP ports, an
// env-var map (string keys must be quoted — this is a generic Jet map
// literal, not string-free sugar), and extra project-relative files layered
// alongside the package binary. `base:` is captured but not yet realized (no
// native registry-pull client exists yet); leaving it unset here keeps this
// fixture buildable end-to-end with `jet image server`.
module image.server {
    kind: .Oci
    from: packages.server
    expose: [8080, 8443]
    env_vars: ["RUST_LOG": "info"]
    files: ["config/app.toml"]
}
